---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CANCEL_SENTENCE } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service | Morium" description="The terms for using Morium's booking, CRM, and invoicing.">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
		<a href="/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">&larr; Back to Morium</a>
		<h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Terms of Service</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/60">Last updated October 27, 2026</p>

		<div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Who we are, and who can use Morium</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Morium is operated by Brock Livermore, doing business as Morium ("Morium," "we," or "us").
					You can reach us, and send any legal notice, at
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					You must be at least 18 years old to use Morium. By creating an account, you confirm that you
					are, and that you have the authority to agree to these terms for your business.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">The service</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Morium is a booking, CRM, and customer-retention platform for mobile
					service businesses. Signing up gets you a booking page, a dashboard,
					invoices and card payments, your team's logins, and (if you have it
					turned on) automatic review-request and rebooking emails for your
					customers.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					To stop scripts from using a booking form to send email to strangers,
					each business's online booking form takes up to 50 requests in any 24
					hours. When it is reached, visitors are asked to call the business and
					the owners get an email. If you need a higher limit for a busy stretch,
					email us.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Your account</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Keep your login private. You are responsible for what happens under
					your account, including what the people you add to your team do. An
					owner can add other owners, who have the same power you do, including
					billing, removing people, and cancelling.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">The "Powered by Morium" link</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Your booking page and embedded booking form show a small "Powered by
					Morium" link to morium.one. Businesses on the Crew plan can turn it off in Settings.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Billing and trials</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Plans are billed monthly. Signing up starts a 14-day free trial.
					We take your card details up front, but you're not charged until the
					trial ends. Cancel any time before then and you're never billed.
					After the trial, your card is charged automatically each month until
					you cancel. Current plans and prices are on the <a href="/pricing" class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">pricing page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Price changes</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We may change our prices. If we do, we will email the account owner at least 30 days
					before the change takes effect for you. A price change never applies to a month you have already
					paid for. If you don't want the new price, you can cancel before it applies to you and you won't
					be charged it. If you don't cancel, the new price applies from your first billing date after the
					change takes effect.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Late or failed payments</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					If a payment doesn't go through, we or our payment provider may email you and may try your card
					again. Your dashboard will show a notice that your payment is past due. We do not pause your
					account automatically. If the payment stays unpaid, we may end your subscription. Your data is not
					deleted when a payment fails (see "After you cancel" below).
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Changing your plan</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					You can change plans in Settings. The app always shows you the exact
					amounts and what will change before you confirm. During your free
					trial, a switch is free and the new price starts when the trial ends.
					After that, moving up can happen right away (you pay the prorated
					difference that day) or on your next billing date, and moving down
					takes effect on your next billing date. Starter covers you plus up to
					5 people. Crew has no limit on team members and lets each person see
					only their own jobs. When Crew changes to Starter, one owner stays, you
					choose one Manager, everyone else becomes an Employee, and custom roles
					stop working.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Card payments from your customers</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					To take card payments, you connect a Stripe account through Morium.
					Your customers pay on a Stripe page and the money goes to your Stripe
					account, not to Morium. You agree to Stripe's{" "}
					<a href="https://stripe.com/legal/connect-account" class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">connected account terms</a>.
					Stripe's standard card fees apply and Morium adds no fee of its own.
					Refunds and disputes on those payments are handled in your Stripe
					account.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Promo codes and discounts</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					A promo code lowers what you pay for Morium. It cannot be exchanged for
					money. Each business can use one promo code, ever, and a code states how
					long its discount lasts.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Your content</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Your content is yours. That means the text, photos, logo, and business details you put into Morium. You give us
					permission to store, copy, and show your content as needed to run Morium and your booking page for you.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">What you upload</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					You must have the right to everything you upload to Morium, such as logos, photos, text, and the
					details of your customers. Don't upload anything that breaks the law, that belongs to someone else
					and that you don't have permission to use, or that breaks these terms.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We can remove an upload that breaks the law or these terms. If it keeps happening, we may suspend
					the account.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Your data</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Your customer data is yours. We don't sell it. Owners can download their
					bookings and customers as spreadsheets in the app, and you can ask us to
					delete your data at any time. See our <a href="/privacy" class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">Privacy Policy</a>.
					You're responsible for having the right to store and contact the
					customers you add.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Emails and acceptable use</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Don't use Morium to send anything your customers haven't agreed to
					receive, or for anything illegal. Review requests and rebook reminders
					are marketing emails: they include an unsubscribe link and your
					business's mailing address, and Morium will not send them until you
					have added a full mailing address (and, for review requests, your Google
					review link). Booking confirmations, reminders, and invoices are
					transactional emails about a booking or payment, and they do not carry
					an unsubscribe link. We can suspend accounts that abuse the platform or
					its automated messaging.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Cancellation</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					{CANCEL_SENTENCE} You can cancel from your account settings or by
					emailing us. There are no cancellation fees on the subscription itself.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					If you cancel at least a day before your next monthly billing date, you
					won't be charged for that upcoming month. If you cancel on or after that
					date, that month has already been billed and isn't refunded, and you keep
					access through the end of it.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">After you cancel</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					When your subscription ends, we keep your business's data so you can come back where you left off.
					We do not delete it automatically. If you want it deleted, or want a copy first, email us and we
					will do it. We may keep a few things if the law requires it. Copies in our backups can take a little longer to disappear. Stripe and our email provider keep their own records under their own
					rules, and we may keep basic billing records, such as invoices to you and your payment history, for
					as long as we need them for taxes and accounting.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">No promise that Morium is always available</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We work hard to keep Morium running, but we don't promise that it will always be available, on
					time, or free of errors. It may be down for maintenance, or because of problems outside our control,
					such as an outage at one of the companies we rely on for hosting, our database, email, or payments.
					Because of that, keep your own way to reach your customers, and don't rely on Morium as the only
					record of your jobs. Owners can download their bookings and customers at any time.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">No warranties ("as is")</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm uppercase">
					Morium is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, either express or
					implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
					non-infringement. We do not promise that Morium will meet your needs, or that it will be
					uninterrupted, secure, or free of errors. Some places do not allow some of these exclusions, so
					some of them may not apply to you.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Limit of liability</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm uppercase">
					To the fullest extent the law allows, Morium and its owner will not be liable for any indirect,
					incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue,
					bookings, customers, or data, arising from your use of Morium, even if we were told they were
					possible. Our total liability for any claim related to Morium will not be more than the greater of
					(a) what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim arose and (b) $100. Nothing in these terms
					limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We are not responsible for what you or your customers do, for the work you do for your customers, or
					for the actions of Stripe or the other companies that provide parts of Morium.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Governing law</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, without regard
					to its conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute about these terms or about Morium will be brought only in
					the state or federal courts located in Collin County, Texas, and you and we agree to those
					courts' authority. Before you file a claim, please email us so we can try to fix it first.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Changes to these terms</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					If these terms change in a meaningful way, we plan to email the address
					on your account before the change takes effect. We update the date at the top of this page
					whenever the terms change.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Questions</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
